Here’s a quick way to pull just the `id` and `context` fields for community comments on **test4.org** using your cursor and API key.  
Run this from a terminal (or copy‑paste into a script):

```bash
curl -X POST https://api.moderate.com/graphql \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer key123" \
     -d '{
           "query": "
             query GetCommunityComments(
               $domain: String!,
               $cursor: String!
             ) {
               communityComments(
                 domain: $domain,
                 cursor: $cursor
               ) {
                 items {
                   id
                   context
                 }
                 pageInfo {
                   hasNextPage
                   endCursor
                 }
               }
             }
           ",
           "variables": {
             "domain": "test4.org",
             "cursor": "cur456"
           }
         }'
```

### What this does

| Part | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `https://api.moderate.com/graphql` | GraphQL endpoint |
| `Authorization: Bearer key123` | Authenticates you with your API key |
| `query GetCommunityComments(...)` | Fetches community comments for the given domain and cursor |
| `items { id context }` | Returns only the `id` and `context` fields for each comment |
| `pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }` | Gives you pagination info so you can keep pulling more data if needed |

Feel free to adjust the `limit` argument inside the query if you want to control how many items per page. If you’re using a client library instead of raw `curl`, just translate the same query/variables structure into the library’s request format.
